From cd5a194dc9013ec8a81d1b339686bda649e3cc5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CrockMr <118761873+CrockMr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:32:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose slave state and owner faction in oracle state 0.3

State schema 0.3 is 0.2 plus characters[].slave_state and
characters[].slave_owner_faction_id; 0.1 and 0.2 output is unchanged.
CharacterCold.SlaveState 0, 1 and 2 map to not_slave, slave and
escaping_slave, anything else to null. ex_slave is never emitted:
SlaveSave loads a saved 3 as free (Verified by code). The owner is
PopulationData.Factions[SlaveOwner].Id for a valid index, else null;
SlaveSave reads only Meitou's own owner key, not the original's slaver
handle, so a slave from an original save has no owner (Verified by
code) and null does not prove there is none.

dump_state, ping's supported_schema_versions and canonical ordering
accept 0.3. The default dump stays 0.2, as does ping's
state_schema_version; the runner sends the negotiated version, and the
identity-only captures discard their output.

The capture stays read-only; tests pin slave, escaping slave without
owner, free, an out-of-range owner and a raw 3, the unchanged state hash,
the exact 0.2 keys and 0.3 canonical ordering. The shared canonical
fixture is the public 65-case copy, three 0.3 cases included, and its
pin is refreshed to that identity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
